WEBVTT

00:00:09.540 --> 00:00:12.160
Wow, you sold seven tickets?

00:00:12.160 --> 00:00:15.870
Yeah. The whole track team's coming to watch.

00:00:15.870 --> 00:00:18.040
I see. That's great.

00:00:18.040 --> 00:00:20.870
Yup. That's great.

00:00:20.870 --> 00:00:23.870
And how many tickets
does the Trianglian have left?

00:00:23.870 --> 00:00:26.580
Lemme see... Eight!

00:00:26.580 --> 00:00:28.750
You've barely sold any.

00:00:28.750 --> 00:00:30.790
How about you, Yuki?

00:00:30.790 --> 00:00:35.500
I have six tickets left. Pretty tough
to sell our quota of ten each.

00:00:35.500 --> 00:00:39.330
Need some help? All mine are gone.

00:00:39.330 --> 00:00:42.580
All?! Expected no less
from Friendly McExtrovert.

00:00:42.580 --> 00:00:44.910
Kaz, you do have many friends.

00:00:44.910 --> 00:00:49.450
Yep! Real struggle every day
replying to all my LIME messages.

00:02:21.330 --> 00:02:23.950
"True Friends"

00:02:23.950 --> 00:02:26.700
"True Friends"
Tonight I have another tale to share with you.

00:02:26.700 --> 00:02:29.450
One of a three-year-old
Ali Baba wetting the bed...

00:02:29.450 --> 00:02:30.540
No!

00:02:30.540 --> 00:02:32.250
You have ten seconds.

00:02:33.160 --> 00:02:36.160
I'll get your damn water, jeez!

00:02:36.160 --> 00:02:38.370
Maybe I rushed into this too fast...

00:02:39.700 --> 00:02:40.950
What do you think?

00:02:40.950 --> 00:02:44.120
Well, they're a little better
than the Spring Troupe.

00:02:45.660 --> 00:02:47.870
But they ain't close to good enough.

00:02:47.870 --> 00:02:50.450
Who's this Yuzo dude?

00:02:50.450 --> 00:02:52.790
He was part of the original Spring Troupe.

00:02:52.790 --> 00:02:54.160
Oh?

00:02:54.160 --> 00:02:57.000
He must be the one Sakuya mentioned.

00:02:57.000 --> 00:02:59.040
Scheherazade!

00:02:59.040 --> 00:03:03.080
The detail in your actin' is lackin'!
Act like the secondary lead.

00:03:03.080 --> 00:03:05.500
Your performance ain't matchin' with Ali Baba's.

00:03:05.500 --> 00:03:07.620
He sounds like the hack.

00:03:07.620 --> 00:03:09.250
Next, Aladdin!

00:03:09.250 --> 00:03:10.750
Y-Yes?

00:03:10.750 --> 00:03:13.250
Your interpretation of your character is weak.

00:03:13.250 --> 00:03:16.120
Don't think you can get by
with just the flirty act.

00:03:16.120 --> 00:03:17.450
Dude, he's brutal.

00:03:17.450 --> 00:03:18.330
Sinbad!

00:03:18.330 --> 00:03:19.790
Y-Yes, sir?

00:03:19.790 --> 00:03:21.660
Both your voice and movements are too damn puny.

00:03:21.660 --> 00:03:24.500
You draw negative attention to yourself!

00:03:24.500 --> 00:03:26.040
I'm sorry.

00:03:26.040 --> 00:03:31.370
The genie... Ain't bad, but you've
gotta solidify your character.

00:03:31.370 --> 00:03:33.080
Oh?

00:03:33.080 --> 00:03:36.540
The biggest problem is Ali Baba.

00:03:36.540 --> 00:03:40.450
You're the lead, but you ain't
got a clue about comedy.

00:03:40.450 --> 00:03:41.700
What do you mean?

00:03:41.700 --> 00:03:45.700
You're too damn serious.
Your pauses are more for drama.

00:03:45.700 --> 00:03:49.040
Watch some stand-up comedy to study up.

00:03:49.040 --> 00:03:51.370
T-Tenten...

00:03:52.910 --> 00:03:54.700
I understand. I'll do that.

00:03:54.700 --> 00:03:56.410
Huh?

00:03:56.410 --> 00:03:58.910
Tenma following directions!

00:03:58.910 --> 00:04:04.160
At any rate, you lot are far from bein' fit
to perform in front of an audience.

00:04:04.160 --> 00:04:07.500
You'll embarrass yourselves
unless you improve before openin' night.

00:04:07.500 --> 00:04:10.910
I agree. Let's have a meeting
to discuss this later.

00:04:10.910 --> 00:04:12.200
Fine, okay.

00:04:12.200 --> 00:04:15.870
Okay, so we'll meet at the lounge after dinner?

00:04:15.870 --> 00:04:18.040
I'll contribute some drinks!

00:04:18.040 --> 00:04:19.620
I'll bring onigiri!

00:04:19.620 --> 00:04:21.370
It's not a party!

00:04:21.370 --> 00:04:24.410
Damn, I wasn't harsh enough.

00:04:24.410 --> 00:04:27.870
They're used to harsh criticism
from Tenma already.

00:04:27.870 --> 00:04:31.250
I like triangles 'cause triangles are triangles!

00:04:31.250 --> 00:04:33.540
I don't get you.

00:04:33.540 --> 00:04:37.370
This bunch'll be interestin'
once they're polished up.

00:04:37.370 --> 00:04:39.370
Is something the matter?

00:04:39.370 --> 00:04:41.750
Nah, it's nothin'.

00:04:46.750 --> 00:04:47.870
What's this?

00:04:47.870 --> 00:04:49.830
An 8mm tape deck player.

00:04:49.830 --> 00:04:51.370
Oh?

00:04:51.370 --> 00:04:52.330
You see, I found this in the storeroom.

00:04:52.330 --> 00:04:55.330
"Summer Troupe First Play's
Start-To-Finish Rehearsal"
You see, I found this in the storeroom.

00:04:55.330 --> 00:04:58.750
It's a recording of the original
Summer Troupe's rehearsal.

00:04:58.750 --> 00:05:00.580
The original Summer Troupe...

00:05:00.580 --> 00:05:04.700
I wanted to show everyone earlier,
but we didn't have a tape deck.

00:05:04.700 --> 00:05:09.540
Yeah, so I borrowed one from
a friend who likes this kinda stuff.

00:05:09.540 --> 00:05:12.410
Sukecchi, pop that into the deck, will ya?

00:05:12.410 --> 00:05:13.700
Sure.

00:05:21.000 --> 00:05:22.290
Isn't that...

00:05:22.290 --> 00:05:24.200
Our rehearsal room?

00:05:24.200 --> 00:05:26.870
Hasn't changed a bit since then.

00:05:28.500 --> 00:05:29.790
Is that man...

00:05:29.790 --> 00:05:32.370
The original troupe's director?

00:05:32.370 --> 00:05:33.750
Dad...

00:05:33.750 --> 00:05:34.700
What?!

00:05:34.700 --> 00:05:36.660
That's your pops?!

00:05:36.660 --> 00:05:39.830
You followed in your dad's
footsteps as director?

00:05:39.830 --> 00:05:41.200
Yeah, kinda.

00:05:41.200 --> 00:05:43.700
Watch. They're about to start.

00:05:48.790 --> 00:05:50.500
Everyone's so good.

00:05:50.500 --> 00:05:52.200
And funny.

00:05:52.200 --> 00:05:55.950
Makes sense why the director wanted us to watch.

00:05:55.950 --> 00:05:57.910
This is the Summer Troupe?

00:05:57.910 --> 00:06:03.080
Yes. They cheered up their audience
and brought out smiles.

00:06:03.080 --> 00:06:06.750
Their strength was in
creating exhilarating comedy.

00:06:10.040 --> 00:06:13.750
But all of them are gone now, right?

00:06:13.750 --> 00:06:16.830
Even though they look like
they're having so much fun acting.

00:06:16.830 --> 00:06:21.500
Sorta makes me sad when I think about it.

00:06:22.370 --> 00:06:24.290
Melancholy.

00:06:26.620 --> 00:06:29.040
That's not gonna happen to us.

00:06:30.910 --> 00:06:35.870
Well, it's over for us if we don't
fill up closing night, though.

00:06:35.870 --> 00:06:38.580
I think we'll be fine, Tenten.

00:06:38.580 --> 00:06:39.950
Me, too!

00:06:39.950 --> 00:06:41.620
I guess so.

00:06:41.620 --> 00:06:44.200
Yeah, we'll be okay.

00:06:49.120 --> 00:06:50.870
That kid...

00:06:55.040 --> 00:06:56.830
Fits great.

00:06:56.830 --> 00:06:58.870
What'd you expect?

00:06:58.870 --> 00:07:01.370
H-How do I look?

00:07:03.370 --> 00:07:04.950
Not bad.

00:07:04.950 --> 00:07:06.950
You look great, too, Yukki!

00:07:06.950 --> 00:07:09.950
Everyone's so floofy and sparkly!

00:07:09.950 --> 00:07:14.620
You look magnificent all together like this!

00:07:14.620 --> 00:07:16.540
You...

00:07:16.540 --> 00:07:19.750
Where'd you find time to make these?

00:07:19.750 --> 00:07:21.790
Little by little after rehearsals.

00:07:21.790 --> 00:07:23.120
After rehearsals?!

00:07:23.120 --> 00:07:25.080
You're amazing, Yuki.

00:07:25.080 --> 00:07:28.250
I'm out like a light after rehearsals.

00:07:28.250 --> 00:07:31.040
Good job, Yuki!

00:07:31.040 --> 00:07:32.580
It was nothing.

00:07:33.580 --> 00:07:37.830
Hey, everyone, I brought in a photographer.

00:07:40.580 --> 00:07:43.250
Hi. I'm Omi Fushimi.

00:07:43.250 --> 00:07:44.330
A photographer?

00:07:44.330 --> 00:07:47.870
Remember I told you I wanted photos
for promotion purposes?

00:07:47.870 --> 00:07:49.700
You went and hired a pro?

00:07:49.700 --> 00:07:52.080
Too bad, but I'm no pro.

00:07:52.080 --> 00:07:54.250
I'm in the photography club at my college.

00:07:54.250 --> 00:07:56.250
Tsuzuru asked me to help.

00:07:57.330 --> 00:08:00.700
We had the manager take photos last time...

00:08:00.700 --> 00:08:02.620
But I rejected that idea quick.

00:08:02.620 --> 00:08:03.910
You did?

00:08:03.910 --> 00:08:08.870
It was rough fixing everything up last time
with the Spring Troupe 'cause the pics sucked.

00:08:08.870 --> 00:08:12.450
Nobody'd be able to tell
how fab Yukki's costumes are.

00:08:12.450 --> 00:08:14.290
Are you sure?

00:08:14.290 --> 00:08:17.370
He's in the photography club and all,
but he's not a pro, right?

00:08:17.370 --> 00:08:21.540
Look who's talking.
You're a middle-school costume designer!

00:08:21.540 --> 00:08:25.330
Well, judge my skill after you see the photos.

00:08:25.330 --> 00:08:28.120
All right, let's get started.

00:08:46.910 --> 00:08:49.370
Ooh, these are sweet!

00:08:49.370 --> 00:08:50.950
So sparkly!

00:08:50.950 --> 00:08:52.080
Well?

00:08:52.080 --> 00:08:56.120
Not bad for a photography club amateur.

00:08:56.120 --> 00:08:57.540
I'm glad.

00:08:58.500 --> 00:09:00.620
Okay, I'll be going now.

00:09:00.620 --> 00:09:04.080
Again, thanks for coming.

00:09:04.080 --> 00:09:08.830
Oh. Do you mind if I take a look
at the theater on my way out?

00:09:13.750 --> 00:09:17.500
Wow, the stage is bigger than expected.

00:09:17.500 --> 00:09:19.750
Are you interested in theater?

00:09:19.750 --> 00:09:21.080
Yes.

00:09:21.080 --> 00:09:24.450
Well, not me, exactly.

00:09:24.450 --> 00:09:26.040
Huh?

00:09:26.040 --> 00:09:30.620
I wanted to take a look to plan ahead.

00:09:32.500 --> 00:09:34.000
Um...

00:09:35.080 --> 00:09:37.450
Take these.

00:09:37.450 --> 00:09:40.870
They're tickets to closing night
as a thank-you for today.

00:09:40.870 --> 00:09:43.250
I hope you'll come watch if you're free.

00:09:44.660 --> 00:09:46.580
Thank you very much.

00:09:48.160 --> 00:09:49.500
Hey, guys!

00:09:49.500 --> 00:09:51.580
Look at this!

00:09:51.580 --> 00:09:52.450
What?

00:09:52.450 --> 00:09:57.000
I updated the Mankai Company website.

00:09:57.000 --> 00:09:58.370
The photos we just took.

00:09:58.370 --> 00:09:59.870
Really jumps out at you.

00:09:59.870 --> 00:10:00.950
Right?

00:10:00.950 --> 00:10:02.580
Triangle windows!

00:10:02.580 --> 00:10:04.450
I made those just for you, Sumi.

00:10:04.450 --> 00:10:05.790
Thanks!

00:10:05.790 --> 00:10:08.830
I'm going live with this
if it looks all right to you.

00:10:08.830 --> 00:10:10.250
Hang on.

00:10:10.250 --> 00:10:11.080
Huh?

00:10:11.080 --> 00:10:13.790
Now what? More complaints?

00:10:13.790 --> 00:10:17.700
No, it's not that.
I'm satisfied with the design.

00:10:17.700 --> 00:10:19.750
The costumes look great in the photos, too.

00:10:19.750 --> 00:10:21.160
Is that a compliment?

00:10:21.160 --> 00:10:25.370
Woot! I got a compliment from Tenten!

00:10:25.370 --> 00:10:29.700
But... can you remove
my face and name from the site?

00:10:29.700 --> 00:10:30.540
Huh?

00:10:30.540 --> 00:10:33.410
What are you talking about?! You're the lead.

00:10:33.410 --> 00:10:38.160
I don't want to rely on
my track record for this play.

00:10:38.160 --> 00:10:42.080
Aw, we'd be sold out in seconds
if we released your name.

00:10:42.080 --> 00:10:44.950
That doesn't really feel right, you know?

00:10:44.950 --> 00:10:46.000
What?!

00:10:46.000 --> 00:10:49.160
Where's the pompous Tenma
who calls himself Mr. High and Mighty?

00:10:49.160 --> 00:10:50.500
I've never said that!

00:10:50.500 --> 00:10:53.000
Well, if that's what Tenten wants.

00:10:53.000 --> 00:10:55.580
Yup, I'm okay with it!

00:10:55.580 --> 00:10:59.450
Okay, let's work together
to sell the remaining tickets!

00:10:59.450 --> 00:11:01.830
So we can't take the easy way?

00:11:01.830 --> 00:11:03.950
Sorry.

00:11:03.950 --> 00:11:08.080
All right! Time to call up my whole crew!

00:11:09.660 --> 00:11:15.660
I am a genie, and I shall grant you
three wishes. Name them.

00:11:15.660 --> 00:11:18.700
Yeowch! My butt's on fire!

00:11:18.700 --> 00:11:20.250
Can't you tell what I want?!

00:11:20.250 --> 00:11:23.120
Do something about the magician and the serpent!

00:11:23.120 --> 00:11:25.540
The magician and the serpent?

00:11:27.910 --> 00:11:31.450
For that scene just now...
It's the highlight of the first act,

00:11:31.450 --> 00:11:34.580
so I'm thinking of adding more action there.

00:11:34.580 --> 00:11:35.790
What do you think?

00:11:35.790 --> 00:11:39.700
Sounds good! I'm down for adding more action!

00:11:39.700 --> 00:11:42.790
I'm not sure about making it so hectic.

00:11:42.790 --> 00:11:44.870
It'll unbalance the whole play.

00:11:44.870 --> 00:11:47.250
Oh, that's true.

00:11:47.250 --> 00:11:51.290
But this is the only scene
the genie has a chance to shine.

00:11:51.290 --> 00:11:54.950
More action will entertain the audience.
I think we should add it.

00:11:54.950 --> 00:11:55.830
Mm-hm.

00:11:55.830 --> 00:11:59.330
But we need to consider
the overall balance of the play.

00:11:59.330 --> 00:12:04.250
The more action we add, the more we lose
the subtler elements of our acting.

00:12:04.250 --> 00:12:05.500
Yeah, for real!

00:12:05.500 --> 00:12:07.540
I wanna do an action scene!

00:12:07.540 --> 00:12:09.910
I wanna watch an action scene!

00:12:09.910 --> 00:12:13.830
You've just been agreeing
with everyone else this whole time.

00:12:13.830 --> 00:12:15.540
What's <i>your </i>opinion?

00:12:15.540 --> 00:12:17.540
Huh? Me?

00:12:17.540 --> 00:12:21.540
Well... I'm cool either way!

00:12:21.540 --> 00:12:22.790
What's that mean?

00:12:22.790 --> 00:12:27.500
Mm, I think it'll be great whether or not
we add the action scene.

00:12:27.500 --> 00:12:29.870
Anyway, things'll work out either way!

00:12:29.870 --> 00:12:31.370
Decide which you like better!

00:12:31.370 --> 00:12:37.080
But I get what Miss Director's saying,
and I think what you're saying is valid.

00:12:37.080 --> 00:12:40.790
So you should just decide with Miss Director.

00:12:40.790 --> 00:12:43.040
Say your own opinion!

00:12:45.790 --> 00:12:49.700
But I'm really okay either way...

00:12:49.700 --> 00:12:52.830
You're just laughing and shrugging it off!

00:12:52.830 --> 00:12:55.250
Hey! That was too much.

00:12:56.620 --> 00:12:57.790
Sorry.

00:12:57.790 --> 00:13:01.830
Let's table the decision
about the action scene for now.

00:13:01.830 --> 00:13:04.370
Let me know if you have
any other opinions about it.

00:13:07.750 --> 00:13:10.250
Hello! We're from Mankai Company!

00:13:10.250 --> 00:13:13.120
Here's a flyer for the Summer
Troupe's debut performance!

00:13:13.120 --> 00:13:13.660
"Known as a Water Dream...
Discover the legendary paradise Oasis!"
Here's a flyer for the Summer
Troupe's debut performance!

00:13:13.660 --> 00:13:15.160
"Known as a Water Dream...
Discover the legendary paradise Oasis!"
<i>Water me!</i>?

00:13:15.160 --> 00:13:17.950
"Known as a Water Dream...
Discover the legendary paradise Oasis!"
Searching for water?

00:13:17.950 --> 00:13:21.620
Yes, it's based on <i>Arabian Nights</i>. Please--

00:13:21.620 --> 00:13:25.620
Hey, come look! God Troupe is doing
a street act over there!

00:13:25.620 --> 00:13:27.750
What?! You think Tasuku and Haruto are there?

00:13:27.750 --> 00:13:30.080
Let's go!

00:13:30.080 --> 00:13:32.160
What's going on?

00:13:32.160 --> 00:13:34.410
Beats me.

00:13:34.410 --> 00:13:42.120
Christine! You're the only light
in the world of darkness I'm trapped in!

00:13:42.120 --> 00:13:44.540
Be gone, Phantom!

00:13:44.540 --> 00:13:47.000
Your world is in the depths of darkness!

00:13:47.000 --> 00:13:49.620
Squee! Haruto!

00:13:49.620 --> 00:13:52.120
Tasuku's so hot!

00:13:54.950 --> 00:13:58.950
God Troupe's performing
<i>The Phantom of the Opera</i>. Come watch.

00:13:58.950 --> 00:14:01.450
Yes! I'll go no matter what!

00:14:01.450 --> 00:14:03.040
My lady...

00:14:04.410 --> 00:14:07.950
Christine, my light.

00:14:10.500 --> 00:14:14.790
He's so cool. Like a prince from a <i>shojo </i>manga!

00:14:14.790 --> 00:14:18.040
He has to stoop that low
to butter up his audience?

00:14:19.040 --> 00:14:21.040
Y-Yuki!

00:14:22.540 --> 00:14:26.160
Hey. You just say something?

00:14:26.160 --> 00:14:28.620
Dunno. You were probably imagining it.

00:14:28.620 --> 00:14:31.000
What theater troupe are you guys from?

00:14:31.000 --> 00:14:32.080
"Recruiting New Troupe Members"
What theater troupe are you guys from?

00:14:32.080 --> 00:14:36.120
"Recruiting New Troupe Members"
Mankai Company? Never heard of it.

00:14:36.120 --> 00:14:38.500
"Recruiting New Troupe Members"
You're pretentious for someone
from a minor troupe.

00:14:38.500 --> 00:14:39.660
You're pretentious for someone
from a minor troupe.

00:14:39.660 --> 00:14:40.950
Whatever.

00:14:40.950 --> 00:14:44.950
I was just amazed that even
popular troupes are so desperate

00:14:44.950 --> 00:14:46.580
that they've got to butter up
their audience like that.

00:14:46.580 --> 00:14:47.870
What?!

00:14:47.870 --> 00:14:49.290
Hey, Haruto.

00:14:49.290 --> 00:14:51.370
What's the commotion?

00:14:59.410 --> 00:15:01.620
Reni!

00:15:01.620 --> 00:15:05.000
Did someone from my troupe cause trouble?

00:15:05.000 --> 00:15:06.120
"My troupe"?

00:15:06.120 --> 00:15:10.000
You're speaking to Reni Kamikizaka,
manager of God Troupe.

00:15:10.000 --> 00:15:12.790
Has Haruto caused you trouble?

00:15:12.790 --> 00:15:14.700
No, it was nothing.

00:15:14.700 --> 00:15:18.370
I apologize. He is a bit hot-blooded.

00:15:18.370 --> 00:15:21.950
You're handing out flyers as well?
For what show?

00:15:21.950 --> 00:15:24.660
Oh, please have one.

00:15:24.660 --> 00:15:25.950
Thanks.

00:15:25.950 --> 00:15:29.410
"Recruiting New Troupe Members"
Ah, <i>Arabian Nights</i>?

00:15:29.410 --> 00:15:31.450
"Recruiting New Troupe Members"

00:15:31.450 --> 00:15:34.410
"Recruiting New Troupe Members"
Mankai Company?

00:15:44.950 --> 00:15:47.500
What's his problem?

00:15:48.910 --> 00:15:51.120
Tasuku, Haruto. Let's go.

00:15:51.120 --> 00:15:52.620
Yes, sir.

00:15:57.370 --> 00:16:01.910
What the heck? Like troupe member, like manager.

00:16:01.910 --> 00:16:07.620
I feel like his attitude changed the moment
he realized we're Mankai Company.

00:16:07.620 --> 00:16:09.370
How rude.

00:16:09.370 --> 00:16:11.870
He probably just realized we're a minor theater.

00:16:11.870 --> 00:16:14.080
Yeah, maybe...

00:16:26.290 --> 00:16:28.080
Kazunari?

00:16:29.120 --> 00:16:31.200
Heya, Miss Director.

00:16:31.200 --> 00:16:35.290
What are you doing out here all alone?

00:16:35.290 --> 00:16:37.370
Just, you know...

00:16:37.370 --> 00:16:40.160
Is it about today?

00:16:41.750 --> 00:16:44.370
Triangle, full marks!

00:16:44.370 --> 00:16:45.750
S-Sumi?!

00:16:45.750 --> 00:16:48.040
What on earth are you doing?!

00:16:48.040 --> 00:16:51.000
I went out to find triangles.

00:16:51.000 --> 00:16:52.160
Huh?

00:16:52.160 --> 00:16:54.290
Shortcut!

00:16:54.290 --> 00:16:56.700
I guess you could call it that...

00:16:56.700 --> 00:16:59.450
What were you guys doing?

00:17:00.500 --> 00:17:04.950
This is a good time.
Can I talk to you both about something?

00:17:08.660 --> 00:17:09.870
You were here?

00:17:09.870 --> 00:17:11.200
Yeah.

00:17:11.200 --> 00:17:13.500
Did you hand out all the flyers?

00:17:13.500 --> 00:17:15.120
Yeah, mostly.

00:17:16.830 --> 00:17:22.750
About today... Did you have to get so angry?

00:17:24.910 --> 00:17:30.500
You see, I was a nerd and had no friends
up until the end of middle school.

00:17:30.500 --> 00:17:31.330
What?

00:17:31.330 --> 00:17:33.000
Kaz was a nerd?

00:17:33.000 --> 00:17:38.620
Yep. Then I turned over a new leaf
in high school and made tons of friends.

00:17:38.620 --> 00:17:41.870
But I was so caught up in upping my friend count

00:17:41.870 --> 00:17:45.410
that I got used to only saying
what pleased others.

00:17:45.410 --> 00:17:48.160
Why won't he say what he really thinks?

00:17:48.160 --> 00:17:50.790
He just didn't want to make waves.

00:17:50.790 --> 00:17:53.120
But wasn't he picky about the photos?

00:17:53.120 --> 00:17:58.120
He made particular requests,
because he had an ideal in mind, right?

00:17:58.120 --> 00:18:01.120
Why doesn't he say anything
when it comes to acting?

00:18:01.120 --> 00:18:05.870
But I decided I couldn't
stay that way after I joined this troupe

00:18:05.870 --> 00:18:08.750
and started acting with everyone.

00:18:08.750 --> 00:18:12.950
If I kept just sucking up to people
and saying stuff that wouldn't offend them,

00:18:12.950 --> 00:18:18.120
I'd never have more than shallow friendships.

00:18:21.750 --> 00:18:26.750
Well... I don't want that.

00:18:26.750 --> 00:18:33.580
I want to connect with everyone
in Summer Troupe on a deeper level.

00:18:38.830 --> 00:18:41.410
I want to connect with you, too, Kaz.

00:18:42.700 --> 00:18:44.250
Sumi...

00:18:44.250 --> 00:18:48.370
And that's not just Misumi.
Everyone feels that way.

00:18:48.370 --> 00:18:50.120
Even Tenma, I'm sure.

00:18:50.120 --> 00:18:55.330
I know he's got a Summer Troupe
that he wants in mind.

00:18:55.330 --> 00:19:00.500
As one who'll be performing alongside him,
I want to hear what he really thinks.

00:19:00.500 --> 00:19:03.830
That's how we'll be more...

00:19:21.160 --> 00:19:22.410
Hey, guys?

00:19:23.410 --> 00:19:26.410
Mind if I say something before we start?

00:19:26.410 --> 00:19:29.660
It's about Sumi's action scene.

00:19:30.750 --> 00:19:32.620
Go ahead.

00:19:32.620 --> 00:19:36.160
This is our debut show,
so I was thinking it'd be best

00:19:36.160 --> 00:19:40.040
to show off our individual personalities.

00:19:40.040 --> 00:19:41.200
Personalities?

00:19:41.200 --> 00:19:44.790
Yeah. You could think of it as an introduction.

00:19:44.790 --> 00:19:49.000
I think it's better to have Sumi, the genie,
flaunt some of his moves.

00:19:49.000 --> 00:19:51.040
And the balance of the whole play?

00:19:51.040 --> 00:19:52.870
That's important, too,

00:19:52.870 --> 00:19:57.620
but I think the audience will love it
if the genie makes a big impact.

00:19:57.620 --> 00:20:00.080
I see.

00:20:00.080 --> 00:20:02.580
What do you think, Director?

00:20:02.580 --> 00:20:05.540
What do <i>you </i>think, Tenma?

00:20:07.950 --> 00:20:10.290
I agree.

00:20:10.290 --> 00:20:14.000
Good. I'll put some thought into that option.

00:20:14.000 --> 00:20:16.870
You <i>can </i>voice your own opinions.

00:20:16.870 --> 00:20:18.870
You should've just said so sooner.

00:20:18.870 --> 00:20:20.500
Got that right.

00:20:27.660 --> 00:20:29.750
Yes?

00:20:29.750 --> 00:20:32.000
May I ask who you are?

00:20:32.000 --> 00:20:34.620
It's nice to meet you.

00:20:35.870 --> 00:20:39.870
I see. You're Tenma's manager?

00:20:39.870 --> 00:20:43.700
What do you want? I thought
I told you never to come here.

00:20:43.700 --> 00:20:48.870
You see, your dad found out
about this theater troupe.

00:20:48.870 --> 00:20:50.870
What?!

00:20:50.870 --> 00:20:53.000
Huh? Hang on!

00:20:53.000 --> 00:20:56.540
Didn't I call your parents when you joined?

00:20:56.540 --> 00:20:59.040
I remember leaving a voicemail...

00:20:59.040 --> 00:21:01.040
That was my number you called.

00:21:01.040 --> 00:21:01.950
Huh?

00:21:01.950 --> 00:21:04.410
Tenma made me keep quiet.

00:21:04.410 --> 00:21:08.410
Igawa is basically my guardian
when my parents are away.

00:21:08.410 --> 00:21:10.160
It shouldn't be an issue.

00:21:10.160 --> 00:21:15.910
You can't get a hold of them when
they're overseas, anyway. It's all the same.

00:21:15.910 --> 00:21:17.500
About that...

00:21:18.450 --> 00:21:20.910
Your father has returned home.

00:21:20.910 --> 00:21:22.040
Wh--?!

00:21:23.040 --> 00:21:27.540
He discovered that you
turned down a movie offer for this,

00:21:27.540 --> 00:21:30.870
and says you should prioritize the movie
over some second-rate play.

00:21:30.870 --> 00:21:35.290
The hell?! He never cared,
but has something to say <i>now</i>?!

00:21:35.290 --> 00:21:39.500
No matter, you still need to
discuss this with your parents!

00:21:40.950 --> 00:21:44.700
Fine. I'll go home for now.

00:21:44.700 --> 00:21:51.290
That's that. My deepest regrets,
but will you begin to search for a replacement--

00:21:51.290 --> 00:21:52.250
What?!

00:21:52.250 --> 00:21:53.410
What the hell are you saying?!

00:21:53.410 --> 00:21:55.200
But your father...

00:21:55.200 --> 00:21:57.370
I'll go and convince him myself.

00:21:57.370 --> 00:21:59.330
Let's get going, Igawa!

00:21:59.330 --> 00:22:00.290
Wait, what?

00:22:00.290 --> 00:22:02.080
Tenten?

00:22:02.080 --> 00:22:05.080
Listen up. Don't you guys worry.

00:22:07.000 --> 00:22:11.160
I'll definitely be on that stage with you guys!
